        title: "PMT creative approval: committee vs. one decision-maker",
        before: "Zach posts the draft ad in a group chat with the owner and six coaches. Five opinions later, the boldest line ('Nobody's born knowing how to ride') becomes 'Professional motorcycle instruction for all skill levels.' The ad sounds like every other ad.",
        after: "ZDub's rule: (1) one approver, the owner; (2) coaches are asked one *input* question: “What do nervous students actually say on day one?”; (3) the owner decides within 48 hours; (4) a strong line can only be cut for being untrue, not for being uncomfortable.",
